# An EXPECTED-DIVERGENCE REGISTER, not a pass.
#
# Every config path below is one this project and `docker compose config`
# genuinely disagree about. The harness asserts the disagreement STILL HAPPENS
# and fails if the set changes in either direction — a fixture that starts
# agreeing is as much a signal as one that starts diverging somewhere new.
#
# It is a register and not a suppression: a divergence listed here is counted,
# printed, and excluded from the pass rate rather than folded into it. A reader
# must not be able to mistake "known and documented" for "agrees".
#
# services.web.environment
#   `environment` is a list in mapping in compose.yaml and a list in
#   compose.override.yaml. Compose normalises both spellings to a mapping and
#   keeps BASE_A. Composure replaces the collection whole, so BASE_A is not in the
#   resolved model. This is deliberate — the model keeps the shape each file
#   wrote so the splice engine addresses real bytes — and it is reported as a
#   `merge-form-mismatch` finding by `composure resolve`, `composure explain` and
#   `composure diagnose`. It is a divergence all the same, and this is where that
#   is written down.
